{"metadata":{"name":"Sahih al Bukhari","section":{"97":{"eng-name":"Oneness, Uniqueness of Allah (Tawheed)","ara-name":"كتاب التوحيد"}},"section_detail":{"97":{"hadithnumber_first":7371,"hadithnumber_last":7563,"arabicnumber_first":7371,"arabicnumber_last":7563}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":7473,"arabicnumber":7473,"text":"Rapporté par Anas bin Malik : Le Messager d’Allah (ﷺ) a dit : « Ad-Dajjal viendra à Médine et trouvera les anges qui la gardent. Si Allah le veut, ni Ad-Dajjal ni la peste ne pourront s’en approcher. »","grades":[{"name":"Imam Bukhari","grade":"Sahih"}],"reference":{"book":97,"hadith":99},"chapter":{"id":31,"ara-name":"باب فِي الْمَشِيئَةِ وَالإِرَادَةِ","eng-name":"(Allah’s) Wish and Will","isFirstHadith":false}}]}